# Writing

- Use **academic-writing** for scientific tone and structure.
- De-AI papers with **academic-humanizer** then **unslop**. Do not use **human-voice** on manuscripts (it casualizes).
- Prefer concrete verbs; cut "utilize", "leverage", "novel framework", "it is worth noting". One claim per paragraph.
- One claim per paragraph; lead with the result when editing Results/Abstract.
- Do not fabricate citations, numbers, or reviewer quotes.
- Prefer concrete verbs; cut "utilize", "leverage", "novel framework", "it is worth noting".
- Preserve LaTeX commands and math; rewrite the words around them.
